                <pb facs="0206" n="140" xml:id="pg140"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3731/665: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-06-13T11:00:00-05:00">June 13, 1934—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>319. Department’s 91, June 12, 5 p.m. Cuban delegates state that a few final
                    requests for concessions (largely minor ones) will be delivered to us
                    tomorrow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
